CREATED:20260707T123806Z
DESCRIPTION:Sponsored by the Rhodes Information Initiative\, the Humanisti
 c AI conference is designed to foster substantive dialogue between the hu
 manities and the sciences.\nThe conference will explore questions such as
 : How might large language models be used to simulate or operationalize h
 istorical knowledge? How is generative AI reshaping concepts such as auth
 orship\, interpretation\, and evidence? And how might current AI models b
 e redesigned to better accommodate humanistic perspectives and theories? 
 \n\n\nREGISTRATION: duke.is/HumAIreg\n\n\nSPEAKERS\n(talk descriptions: d
 uke.is/HumAIspeakers)\n\nLauren F. Klein\nOn Models and Marbles: Reasonin
 g and interpretation in the Age of AI\n\nEamon Duede:\nThis talk examines
  intellectual distance and impact across the sciences and humanities\, an
 d considers how AI may shape the future of humanistic scholarship.\n\nHoy
 t Long\nExperiments in mindless reading with LLMs\n\nEmily Kadens\nUsing 
 AI to automate the structuring of historical data\n\nMaria Antoniak\nThe 
 Garden of Forking Prompts: How users explore narrative space in story gen
 eration\n\nTed Underwood\nChronoLogic: How do we know whether LLMs can re
 present the past?
DURATION:P1DT4H
DTSTAMP:20260909T202637Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260925T080000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260909T202637Z
