DESCRIPTION:Welcome Class of 2030!\nPresented by Duke's Office of Informat
 ion Technology and partners\, Duke Tech Week\, Sept. 28 and Oct. 1\, is d
 esigned to help students learn about the technology resources available t
 o them throughout their time at Duke. \n\nWe'll be tabling on the plaza f
 or the kickoff of Duke Tech Week. Between interactive demos\, giveaways a
 nd snacks\, students will find guidance on keeping their devices safe and
  data secure\; how to get support for laptops\, ID cards\, and Duke softw
 are\; opportunities to sharpen their technology skills at the Innovation 
 Co-Lab\; and information on co-curricular programs such as Code+\; and on
  purchasing tech essentials at the Duke Technology Center.\n\nThe day wil
 l feature activities such as:\n\nExploring AI in Student Life - Dig deepe
 r into Duke's suite of AI tools.\nLock-Picking Station - Learn about the 
 importance of staying secure.\nMatch the Studio - The Bryan Center Studio
 s will challenge you to match the activity with the right studio.\nEnter 
 the Portal - Take a spin with DukeMobile for an AirTag or Anker power ban
 k. \nScavenger Hunt - Find the tech locations on campus to win an exclusi
 ve t-shirt.\nInstagram Giveaway - Enter for a chance to win a tech prize.
  Follow @dukeoit on Instagram for details.\nRandom daily giveaways - Swin
 g by to win!
DURATION:PT4H
