CONTACT;X-BEDEWORK-UID=00f1fcdb-0f068baf-010f-068baf83-00000004:None
CREATED:20260911T154247Z
DESCRIPTION:Focusing on the role that deportation defense lawyers play in 
 legitimizing the deportation regime\, this talk addresses the responsibil
 ities lawyers have when representing people within an unjust legal system
 . What does it mean for an immigration lawyer to genuinely earn the trust
  of undocumented communities and become an abogade de confianza? Borja ex
 plores how lawyers can work alongside families\, community organizers\, a
 nd participatory defense campaigns to challenge detention and deportation
 . So doing\, they can help center the leadership of criminalized people b
 y supporting mutual aid efforts\, court watch projects\, and freedom camp
 aigns. Borja's public talk casts light on what effective immigration advo
 cacy can look like and encourages us to rethink the conventional wisdom t
 hat good legal representation alone is enough to produce justice.\n\nYvet
 te Borja is an Acting Assistant Professor of Lawyering at NYU Law. A prev
 ious inaugural Laura E. Gómez Teaching Fellow on Latinx People and the La
 w at UCLA School of Law\, Borja has published articles in the UCLA Chican
 x Latinx Law Review and the NYU Journal of lnternational Law and Politics
 . Borja hosts and produces the Radio Cachimbona podcast\, which has over 
 180\,000 total downloads. Apple Podcasts featured Radio Cachimbona for La
 tinx Heritage Month and Women's History Month.
DURATION:PT1H30M
DTSTAMP:20260911T160224Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260928T123000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260911T160224Z
