DESCRIPTION:WHAT: Postdoc Research Communication Series: The Art of Resear
 ch Communication\nWHEN: Tues Sept 29\, Tues Oct 6\, and Tues Oct 13\, 11 
 am - 12 pm\nREGISTER: https://sites.duke.edu/mentoringandcommunication/\n
 \nSure\, your research on fill-in-the-blank is fascinating and important\
 , but in order to help the public understand why it matters (and why they
  should support it!)\, you need to be able to communicate what you do in 
 ways that are clear and engaging. In this 3-part series\, noted Research 
 Communication expert Jory Weintraub PhD will teach you how to communicate
  your research effectively\, no matter what field you are in - Humanities
 \, Social Sciences\, or STEM. \n\nSession 1: Research Communication Funda
 mentals\, Tues Sept 29\, 11 am-12 pm\nThis activity-based session will in
 troduce the fundamentals of research communication.\n\nSession 2: Communi
 cating Your Research Through Storytelling\, Tues Oct 6\, 11 am-12 pm\nRes
 earch demonstrates that people learn new information more effectively\, u
 nderstand it better and remember it longer when it is delivered in the fo
 rm of a story. In this session\, we'll dig more deeply into this and disc
 uss the elements of great storytelling.\n  \nSession 3: Engaging the Publ
 ic in Your Research Through Outreach\, Tues Oct 13\, 11 am-12 pm\nOnce yo
 u've learned the fundamentals of research communication and how to tell t
 he story of your work\, it's time to apply these skills by engaging the p
 ublic through outreach. This session will introduce and explore strategie
 s for outreach\, and participants will develop their own outreach plan.\n
 \nSpeaker: Jory Weintraub PhD is Director of Science Engagement at NC Sta
 te University. From 2015-2022 he was Science Communication Director with 
 Duke Science & Society and taught undergraduate and graduate courses in s
 cience communication. He received a PhD in Immunology\, did a postdoc in 
 STEM education\, and has spent the last 25 years doing\, teaching and coa
 ching science communication and outreach.
DURATION:PT1H
